## Answer

When the module-level `defaultZone` is `null`, `Settings.defaultZone` returns **`LocalZone.instance`** — i.e. the `LocalZone` singleton (a `Zone` subclass instance, `type === "local"`, `isValid === true`). It does **not** return `null`, `undefined`, or throw.

Note: `Settings.defaultZone` does **not** call `normalizeZone` at all. `normalizeZone` is only called by the *setter* (`Settings.defaultZoneName`) and elsewhere in the codebase.

## Verbatim source

`/luxon/src/settings.js` (lines 7-12, module state):
```js
let now = () => Date.now(),
  defaultZone = null, // not setting this directly to LocalZone.instance bc loading order issues
  defaultLocale = null,
  defaultNumberingSystem = null,
  defaultOutputCalendar = null,
  throwOnInvalid = false;
```

Getter (`/luxon/src/settings.js`, lines 57-63):
```js
  /**
   * Get the default time zone object to create DateTimes in. Does not affect existing instances.
   * @type {Zone}
   */
  static get defaultZone() {
    return defaultZone || LocalZone.instance;
  }
```

Setter (`/luxon/src/settings.js`, lines 45-55):
```js
  /**
   * Set the default time zone to create DateTimes in. Does not affect existing instances.
   * @type {string}
   */
  static set defaultZoneName(z) {
    if (!z) {
      defaultZone = null;
    } else {
      defaultZone = normalizeZone(z);
    }
  }
```

`normalizeZone` helper (`/luxon/src/impl/zoneUtil.js`, lines 12-36) — called by the setter, not the getter:
```js
export function normalizeZone(input, defaultZone) {
  let offset;
  if (isUndefined(input) || input === null) {
    return defaultZone;
  } else if (input instanceof Zone) {
    return input;
  } else if (isString(input)) {
    const lowered = input.toLowerCase();
    if (lowered === "local") return defaultZone;
    else if (lowered === "utc" || lowered === "gmt") return FixedOffsetZone.utcInstance;
    else if ((offset = IANAZone.parseGMTOffset(input)) != null) {
      // handle Etc/GMT-4, which V8 chokes on
      return FixedOffsetZone.instance(offset);
    } else if (IANAZone.isValidSpecifier(lowered)) return IANAZone.create(input);
    else return FixedOffsetZone.parseSpecifier(lowered) || new InvalidZone(input);
  } else if (isNumber(input)) {
    return FixedOffsetZone.instance(input);
  } else if (typeof input === "object" && input.offset && typeof input.offset === "number") {
    // This is dumb, but the instanceof check above doesn't seem to really work
    // so we're duck checking it
    return input;
  } else {
    return new InvalidZone(input);
  }
}
```

`LocalZone.instance` (`/luxon/src/zones/localZone.js`, lines 15-20) lazily creates the singleton:
```js
  static get instance() {
    if (singleton === null) {
      singleton = new LocalZone();
    }
    return singleton;
  }
```

